package views

templ Terms(){
    @HeaderCustomTitle("Terms of Service", "https://cyphergoat.com/terms", "CypherGoat's Terms of Service, covering the nature of our rate comparison service, prohibited uses, sanctions restrictions and partner compliance obligations."){

    }
<style>
    body {
        background-color: #0b0d14;
        font-family: 'Inter', 'Segoe UI', 'Arial', sans-serif;
    }

    .legal-shell {
        max-width: 1100px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 3.25rem 1.5rem 0;
    }

    .legal-hero {
        max-width: 52rem;
        margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .legal-card {
        padding: 2rem;
        border-radius: 24px;
        border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
        background:
            linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.018), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.008)),
            #11151c;
        box-shadow: 0 28px 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
    }

    .legal-list {
        display: grid;
        gap: 1rem;
    }

    .legal-item {
        padding-top: 1.4rem;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    }

    .legal-item:first-child {
        padding-top: 0;
        border-top: none;
    }

    .legal-item strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
        .legal-shell {
            padding: 2.5rem 1rem 0;
        }

        .legal-card {
            padding: 1.4rem;
            border-radius: 18px;
        }
    }
      
    </style>
    <div class="legal-shell text-gray-100 font-sans">
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-400">These terms govern your access to and use of the CypherGoat website, interface and API. Please read them before using the service.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">Last updated: September 8, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <ul class="legal-card legal-list max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">1. Nature of the Service:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat is a rate comparison and routing interface. We display live quotes from independent third-party exchange providers and pass your instructions to the provider you select.</p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">CypherGoat does not operate an exchange. We do not buy cryptocurrency from users, we do not sell cryptocurrency to users, we do not exchange fiat currency for digital assets, and we do not provide a digital asset exchange, brokerage, transfer or custody service. Every trade is executed by the third-party provider you choose, under that provider's own terms and its own regulatory obligations.</p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">Nothing on this website constitutes legal, financial, investment or tax advice, and it should not be relied on as such in any circumstance.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">2. No Custody of Funds:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat does not, at any point, take custody of your funds. We do not receive, hold, pool, transmit or control user assets at any stage of a swap. Funds move directly between you and the exchange provider you select. Because we never hold or transmit funds, we are not in a position to screen, freeze, delay or reverse a transaction once it has been submitted to a provider.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">3. Eligibility and Prohibited Jurisdictions:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">You must be at least 18 years old to use CypherGoat. We do not knowingly provide services to minors.</p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">By using CypherGoat you represent and warrant that you are not a citizen or resident of, and are not located in, any country or territory subject to comprehensive United Nations sanctions, sanctions administered by the United States Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC), or equivalent measures. You further represent that you are not a person or entity named on any applicable sanctions list, that you are not acting on behalf of any such person or entity, and that your use of the service does not breach any law applicable to you.</p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">Comprehensively sanctioned jurisdictions currently include: Cuba, Iran, North Korea, Syria, and the Crimea, Donetsk, Luhansk, Zaporizhzhia and Kherson regions of Ukraine. Additional restrictions apply to Afghanistan, Belarus, Burma (Myanmar), Central African Republic, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Eritrea, Haiti, Iraq, Lebanon, Libya, Mali, Nicaragua, Russia, Somalia, South Sudan, Sudan, Venezuela, Yemen and Zimbabwe. This list is maintained for guidance and may not reflect the most recent changes to applicable sanctions programmes. You remain responsible for determining the rules that apply to you.</p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">Deposit and destination addresses identified as sanctioned are refused.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">4. Prohibited Uses:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">You may use CypherGoat only for lawful purposes. CypherGoat has zero tolerance for use of the service for any illegal purpose. You agree not to use the service:</p>
        <ul class="text-base text-gray-300 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside mt-3">
          <li>In any way that breaches any applicable national, federal, state, local or international law or regulation.</li>
          <li>To launder the proceeds of crime, to finance terrorism, or to evade sanctions, export controls or tax obligations.</li>
          <li>To transact in funds you know or suspect to be derived from criminal activity, fraud, theft, ransomware or the exploitation of another person.</li>
          <li>To disguise the origin, source, ownership or control of assets in order to defeat a lawful enquiry.</li>
          <li>To breach, or to attempt to breach, the terms of any third-party provider you reach through CypherGoat.</li>
          <li>To exploit or harm minors in any way.</li>
          <li>To impersonate CypherGoat, a member of CypherGoat staff, or any other person or entity.</li>
          <li>To introduce malicious code, or to gain or attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the service or any connected system.</li>
          <li>To use any robot, scraper or automated process to access the service other than through our documented public API.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">5. Partner Exchanges and AML Compliance:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">The providers listed on CypherGoat are independent businesses responsible for their own regulatory compliance. Providers monitor incoming transactions in order to meet their anti-money laundering (AML) and counter-terrorist financing obligations, and may request identity verification (KYC) where their policies or the law require it. We support our partners in meeting those obligations in full, and we do not assist any user in avoiding them.</p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">Where a provider has published its verification practices, we surface that information on the quote screen so you can make an informed choice about who you transact with. This information is descriptive, is provided by the partner, and cannot be treated as a guarantee. A provider may request verification in any transaction at its discretion or where required by law, regardless of what is displayed. Before transacting you should read the terms of use and privacy policy of the provider you intend to use.</p>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">CypherGoat does not execute trades, does not hold funds, and is not in a position to perform transaction screening or customer verification itself. Where a provider requires information from you in order to release funds, that matter is between you and the provider.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">6. Third-Party Providers:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat facilitates communication with third-party providers. You must understand and accept the risks, terms and privacy policies of any provider you use. CypherGoat bears no responsibility for the actions, omissions, solvency or outcomes of these providers, and links to third-party sites are provided for convenience only.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">7. Partner Selection and Ongoing Review:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">We carry out due diligence on providers before integrating them and review them on an ongoing basis. We may suspend or remove a provider at any time. Our partner assessment and monitoring process is described in our <a href="/aml-policy" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white underline">Compliance and AML Policy</a>.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">8. Investment Risks:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">Digital assets are volatile and trading them carries risk, including total loss. You are solely responsible for your own decisions. CypherGoat does not provide investment advice or recommendations.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">9. Tax Matters:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">You are solely responsible for determining and meeting any tax obligations arising from your transactions. CypherGoat does not calculate, withhold or report taxes on your behalf.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">10. On-Chain Fees:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">On-chain transactions may incur network fees, such as gas fees on Ethereum. These fees are set by the relevant blockchain network, vary with network conditions, and are your responsibility. CypherGoat does not receive them.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">11. No Responsibility for Loss:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">To the fullest extent permitted by law, CypherGoat is not responsible for any loss of funds or assets arising from your use of the service or your dealings with third-party providers. The service is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without warranties of any kind. You assume full responsibility for your decisions and their outcomes.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">12. Enforcement and Investigation of Abuse:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">We reserve the right to investigate suspected breaches of these terms, including any breach arising from a transaction you create or submit to a provider. Where we consider it appropriate we may refuse a request, block access to the interface, withhold participation in optional programmes, or take other corrective action, in each case without notice. We may report activity to the relevant authorities where we are required or permitted to do so.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">13. Law Enforcement Enquiries:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat responds to validly issued legal process served through proper channels, and will cooperate with lawful requests from competent authorities. Other requests are considered case by case at our discretion. Enquiries should be sent to <a href="mailto:compliance@cyphergoat.com" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white underline">compliance@cyphergoat.com</a>. Details of the limited data we hold, and for how long, are set out in our <a href="/privacy" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white underline">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">14. Geographic Restrictions:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">The service may not be lawfully available in every jurisdiction. We make no representation that the service is appropriate or available for use in any particular location. If you access the service you do so on your own initiative and are responsible for compliance with your local law. Where a competent authority or a partner notifies us through proper channels that a user is circumventing or attempting to circumvent geographic restrictions, we will take the steps needed to comply.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="legal-item">
        <strong class="text-white text-xl">15. Changes to These Terms:</strong>
        <p class="text-base text-gray-300">We may revise these terms from time to time. Changes take effect when posted, and your continued use of the service after that point means you accept them. Please check this page periodically.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="text-base text-center text-gray-400 mt-8">By using CypherGoat you acknowledge and agree to these terms. Questions and concerns can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@cyphergoat.com" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white underline">support@cyphergoat.com</a>, and compliance matters to <a href="mailto:compliance@cyphergoat.com" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white underline">compliance@cyphergoat.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
  @Footer(){}
}

templ Privacy(){
    @HeaderCustomTitle("Privacy Policy", "https://cyphergoat.com/privacy", "CypherGoat's Privacy Policy: what limited data we collect, how long we retain it, and when it is disclosed to competent authorities."){

    }
<style>
    body {
   background-color: #0b0d14;
    font-family: 'Inter', 'Segoe UI', 'Arial', sans-serif;
    }
</style>
<div class="legal-shell text-gray-100 font-sans">
    <header class="legal-hero">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-400">This policy sets out what information CypherGoat collects, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and the circumstances in which it is disclosed.</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">Last updated: September 8, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <ul class="legal-card legal-list max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">1. Information We Collect:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat does not collect personal information unless explicitly provided by the user. Any data collected is limited to what is necessary to provide our services.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">2. Use of Information:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">We use the information you provide solely to facilitate the services offered by CypherGoat. We do not sell, rent, or share your information with third parties, except as required by law or to fulfill service requests.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">3. Third-Party Services:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat integrates with third-party providers to facilitate transactions. These providers may have their own privacy policies, and we encourage users to review them before engaging with their services.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">4. Cookies and Tracking:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat may use cookies or similar technologies for affiliate tracking. These cookies do not store personal information and can be disabled in your browser settings.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">5. Data Security:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">We implement industry-standard security measures to protect your data. However, no system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee the absolute security of your information.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">6. Data Retention and Logging:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">We keep records of the transactions created through our interface. Transaction data, including destination addresses and amounts, is retained for 14 days and is then anonymised.</p>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">Several partner exchanges require us to capture and retain connection metadata in order to meet their own compliance obligations. Where a trade is initiated through such a partner, we record and retain:</p>
            <ul class="text-base text-gray-300 space-y-1 list-disc list-inside">
                <li><strong>IP address</strong></li>
                <li><strong>User agent</strong></li>
                <li><strong>Language preferences</strong></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">These records are held securely for the period required by the relevant partner's policy, which may exceed 14 days. For interactions that do not involve such a partner, we do not retain IP addresses, user agents or language preferences.</p>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">Records are retained so that we can respond to lawful requests and support partner compliance enquiries. They are never sold, rented or shared for marketing purposes.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">7. Disclosure to Authorities and Partners:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat discloses information in response to validly issued legal process served through proper channels, and cooperates with lawful requests from competent authorities. We also respond to compliance enquiries from partner exchanges relating to a specific transaction where we are satisfied the request is legitimate. Disclosure is always made on an individual, case-by-case basis, never in bulk. Requests should be directed to <a href="mailto:compliance@cyphergoat.com" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white underline">compliance@cyphergoat.com</a>.</p>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">Partner exchanges operate their own data practices and may retain information about amounts, assets, addresses and transaction hashes independently of us. We encourage you to review the privacy policy of any provider before transacting.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">8. Open Source Transparency:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoats web interface is open source, allowing anyone review the code and verify how user data is handled. This transparency ensures that our privacy practices align with the policy outlined here. You can access the source code on our public repository <a href="https://github.com/cyphergoat/web">here</a>.</p>
        </li>
                <li class="legal-item">
            <strong class="text-white text-xl">9. Changes to This Policy:</strong>
            <p class="text-base text-gray-300">CypherGoat reserves the right to update this Privacy Policy at any time. Changes will be communicated through our platform, and continued use of our services constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
        </li>

    </ul>
    

    <p class="text-base text-center text-gray-400 mt-8">Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@cyphergoat.com" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white underline">support@cyphergoat.com</a>. Legal and compliance requests should go to <a href="mailto:compliance@cyphergoat.com" class="text-gray-300 hover:text-white underline">compliance@cyphergoat.com</a>.</p>
</div>


@Footer(){}

}

templ CGShield(){
    @HeaderCustomTitle("CypherGoat Shield Program", "https://cyphergoat.com/cyphergoat-shield", "CypherGoat Shield: a discretionary programme covering execution failure by partner exchanges. Excludes AML, sanctions and law enforcement holds."){}

    <style>
    body {
        background-color: #0b0d14;
        font-family: 'Inter', 'Segoe UI', 'Arial', sans-serif;
    }
    .shield-icon {
        color: #FFD700;
        margin-right: 8px;
    }
    .section-card {
        background:
            linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.018), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.008)),
            #11151c;
        border-radius: 24px;
        padding: 24px;
        margin-bottom: 24px;
        border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
        box-shadow: 0 28px 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
    }
    .highlight {
        color: #f3eee2;
        font-weight: 500;
    }
    </style>

    <div class="legal-shell text-gray-100 font-sans py-12 px-6">
        <header class="mb-16 text-center max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
                <svg class="w-10 h-10 text-yellow-400 mr-3" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                    <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.166 4.999A11.954 11.954 0 0010 1.944 11.954 11.954 0 0017.834 5c.11.65.166 1.32.166 2.001 0 5.225-3.34 9.67-8 11.317C5.34 16.67 2 12.225 2 7c0-.682.057-1.35.166-2.001zm11.541 3.708a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                </svg>
                <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white">CypherGoat Shield</h1>
            </div>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-300 mt-4">CypherGoat Shield covers execution failure by a partner exchange. When you see the Shield icon next to an exchange, your transaction is covered by the guarantee set out below, subject to the exclusions in section 3.</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">Last updated: September 8, 2026</p>
        </header>

        <div class="space-y-10 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="section-card">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. What is the CypherGoat Shield Guarantee?</h2>
                <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">CypherGoat Shield covers execution failure. If you complete a transaction and the exchange neither delivers your funds nor refunds you, we will step in to help. Where the exchange cannot provide a legitimate reason for withholding settlement, CypherGoat will reimburse you up to the covered amount.</p>
                <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">Shield addresses unfair or failed execution. It is not insurance against compliance action. Where an exchange withholds funds because of an anti-money laundering determination, a sanctions match, a legal order or a law enforcement request, that is a legitimate reason and Shield does not apply. If an exchange reports that it suspects you are a sanctioned person or entity, we will need to establish that you are not before any payment can be made.</p>
                <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">Shield is a discretionary programme offered free of charge. It is not paid insurance, it does not cover every possible situation, and the final disbursement amount is at CypherGoat's sole discretion. We may change the available coverage for new transactions or discontinue the programme at any time.</p>
                
                <div class="bg-white/[0.03] p-4 rounded-[18px] mt-4 border border-white/8">
                    <p class="text-base text-gray-200"><span class="font-bold">How to Check Coverage:</span> The protection amount is set by each exchange. You can see the exact amount covered directly next to the <span class="font-bold">Shield icon</span> in the exchange listing before you start your trade. This amount is locked in for you the moment you begin your transaction.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="section-card">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. How to Make a Claim</h2>
                <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">We keep the process as simple as possible:</p>
                
                <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
                    <div class="flex">
                        <span class="bg-[#f3eee2] text-[#0b0d14] rounded-full w-6 h-6 flex items-center justify-center mr-3 flex-shrink-0">1</span>
                        <p class="text-base text-gray-300"><span class="font-semibold text-white">Contact Us:</span> If you have a problem, you must contact our support team within <span class="highlight">four (4) weeks</span> of creating your transaction. Please provide your CypherGoat Transaction ID and explain the issue. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:support@cyphergoat.com" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white hover:underline">support@cyphergoat.com</a>.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="flex">
                        <span class="bg-[#f3eee2] text-[#0b0d14] rounded-full w-6 h-6 flex items-center justify-center mr-3 flex-shrink-0">2</span>
                        <p class="text-base text-gray-300"><span class="font-semibold text-white">Mediation:</span> We will first talk to the exchange on your behalf to try and solve the problem directly. Our goal is always to get your transaction completed or refunded by the exchange.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="flex">
                        <span class="bg-[#f3eee2] text-[#0b0d14] rounded-full w-6 h-6 flex items-center justify-center mr-3 flex-shrink-0">3</span>
                        <p class="text-base text-gray-300"><span class="font-semibold text-white">Reimbursement:</span> If we can't solve the issue and the exchange doesn't provide a good reason for holding the funds, we will process your refund. The reimbursement will be for your lost amount, up to the covered limit that was shown when you started the trade. Please keep in mind the whole process can take a week or longer.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="section-card">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. What Is NOT Covered</h2>
                <p class="text-base text-gray-300 mt-3">The CypherGoat Shield is here to protect you from unfair practices, but it doesn't cover every situation. Please understand that the guarantee <span class="font-bold">does not apply</span> to:</p>
                
                <ul class="text-base text-gray-300 space-y-3 mt-4 pl-6">
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM8.707 7.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414L8.586 10l-1.293 1.293a1 1 0 101.414 1.414L10 11.414l1.293 1.293a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11.414 10l1.293-1.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L10 8.586 8.707 7.293z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span><span class="font-semibold text-white">High AML Risk:</span> Transactions that are blocked by the exchange because they have a high Anti-Money Laundering (AML) risk score.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM8.707 7.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414L8.586 10l-1.293 1.293a1 1 0 101.414 1.414L10 11.414l1.293 1.293a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11.414 10l1.293-1.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L10 8.586 8.707 7.293z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span><span class="font-semibold text-white">Prohibited Sources:</span> Funds that come from crypto mixers, tumblers, or sanctioned addresses (like those on the OFAC list).</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM8.707 7.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414L8.586 10l-1.293 1.293a1 1 0 101.414 1.414L10 11.414l1.293 1.293a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11.414 10l1.293-1.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L10 8.586 8.707 7.293z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span><span class="font-semibold text-white">Legal Orders:</span> Funds that are frozen because of a request from the police or a court order.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM8.707 7.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414L8.586 10l-1.293 1.293a1 1 0 101.414 1.414L10 11.414l1.293 1.293a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11.414 10l1.293-1.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L10 8.586 8.707 7.293z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span><span class="font-semibold text-white">User Error:</span> Mistakes like sending crypto to the wrong address or choosing the wrong network.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM8.707 7.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414L8.586 10l-1.293 1.293a1 1 0 101.414 1.414L10 11.414l1.293 1.293a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11.414 10l1.293-1.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L10 8.586 8.707 7.293z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span><span class="font-semibold text-white">Stolen Funds:</span> The program does not cover funds stolen from your personal wallet or accounts.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-start">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-red-500 mr-2 mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zM8.707 7.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414L8.586 10l-1.293 1.293a1 1 0 101.414 1.414L10 11.414l1.293 1.293a1 1 0 001.414-1.414L11.414 10l1.293-1.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L10 8.586 8.707 7.293z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span><span class="font-semibold text-white">Late Claims:</span> Any problems reported to us more than four weeks after the transaction was made.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            
            <div class="section-card">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. Important Points to Remember</h2>
                <ul class="text-base text-gray-300 space-y-3 mt-3">
                    <li class="flex items-center">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-yellow-400 mr-2 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2h-1V9a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span>Our guarantee <span class="font-bold">does not</span> cover funds blocked for AML, sanctions, legal or law enforcement reasons.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-center">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-yellow-400 mr-2 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2h-1V9a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span>We always try to solve your issue with the exchange first before issuing a refund.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-center">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-yellow-400 mr-2 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2h-1V9a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span>The <span class="font-bold">4-week deadline</span> to report an issue is firm.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex items-center">
                        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-yellow-400 mr-2 flex-shrink-0" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2h-1V9a1 1 0 00-1-1z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                        </svg>
                        <span><span class="font-bold">Always check the coverage amount</span> next to the Shield icon before you trade.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="text-center mt-16 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-[#161a24] border border-[#1e2235] rounded-lg p-6">
                <p class="text-lg text-white">Our mission with CypherGoat Shield is to create a safer and more trustworthy trading environment for everyone.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @Footer(){}
}
